545	#[cfg(feature = "alloc")]
546	#[cfg_attr(docsrs, doc(cfg(feature = "alloc")))]
547	impl<T: CCell, P: CLenAlloc> CBox<T, CAllocator<P>> {
548	    /// The object as a `Box<T, CAllocator<P>>`: the same pointer and
549	    /// allocator, nothing copied — `CBox` → `Box`, once C no longer keeps
550	    /// the object. The box drops it in place and frees it through the
551	    /// family, as this `CBox` would have.
552	    ///
553	    /// Zero-sized and over-aligned `T` are refused at compile time, as by
554	    /// [`CBox::from`].
555	    ///
556	    /// # Safety
557	    ///
558	    /// A `Box` lends `&T` and `&mut T`, through which safe code moves the
559	    /// object's bytes (`mem::swap`, `mem::replace`) and reads them under a
560	    /// shared reference. So:
561	    ///
562	    /// - the object must not be address-sensitive: neither C nor the object
563	    ///   itself may hold a pointer into it (C registered it, or it points
564	    ///   into itself), as for a value [`define_ctype!`](crate::define_ctype)'s
565	    ///   layout type holds by value;
